Book3264Examples -- Examples using M2 and Schubert2 to do intersection theory
*****************************************************************************

Description
===========

This package consists almost entirely of example code for the main text and
exercises of the book '3264 \& All That: Intersection Theory in Algebraic
Geometry' by Eisenbud and Harris.  Most of the example code relies on the
package *note Schubert2: (Schubert2)Top,.  The information in this package is
best accessed via the *note help: (Macaulay2Doc)help, or *note viewHelp:
(Macaulay2Doc)viewHelp, commands.

Conventions in effect throughout:

-Blackboard bold is represented in code by doubling a letter, so for example
G(2,4) and GG(1,3) are both the Grassmannian of lines in ${\mathbb P}^3$.

* Menu:


Chapter 4
* Intersection Theory Section 4.1: Intersection Theory Section 4_pd1.  The coordinate ring of the Grassmannian
* Intersection Theory Section 4.2: Intersection Theory Section 4_pd2.  The Chow ring of GG(1,3)
* Intersection Theory Section 4.3: Intersection Theory Section 4_pd3.  Schubert calculus in general

Chapter 5
* Intersection Theory Section 5.2: Intersection Theory Section 5_pd2.  Basics of vector bundles and Chern classes
* Intersection Theory Section 5.3: Intersection Theory Section 5_pd3.  Operations on vector bundles
* Intersection Theory Section 5.4.1-2: Intersection Theory Section 5_pd4_pd1-2.  Chern class computations on projective space
* Intersection Theory Section 5.4.3: Intersection Theory Section 5_pd4_pd3.  Tangent bundles to hypersurfaces
* Intersection Theory Section 5.4.4: Intersection Theory Section 5_pd4_pd4.  Bundles on Grassmannians

