Intersection Theory Section 5.2 -- Basics of vector bundles and Chern classes
*****************************************************************************

In Schubert2, a vector bundle (or more generally, an *note AbstractSheaf:
(Schubert2)AbstractSheaf,) is given by two pieces of data: its Chern classes
and its rank.  Schubert2 has many built-in bundles for common varieties.  For
example, a Grassmannian G comes with its universal subbundle and quotient
bundle stored in G.Bundles:

+------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : G = flagBundle({2,3})                      |
|                                                |
|o1 = G                                          |
|                                                |
|o1 : a flag bundle with subquotient ranks {2..3}|
+------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : (S,Q) = G.Bundles                          |
|                                                |
|o2 = (S, Q)                                     |
|                                                |
|o2 : Sequence                                   |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : S                                          |
|                                                |
|o3 = S                                          |
|                                                |
|o3 : an abstract sheaf of rank 2 on G           |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : Q                                          |
|                                                |
|o4 = Q                                          |
|                                                |
|o4 : an abstract sheaf of rank 3 on G           |
+------------------------------------------------+

The Chern classes of a vector bundle are accessed using the *note chern:
(Schubert2)chern, command:

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : chern(1,Q) -- The first Chern class of Q                                |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = H                                                                       |
|      2,1                                                                    |
|                                                                             |
|                                            QQ[][H   ..H   , H   ..H   ]     |
|                                                  1,1   1,2   2,1   2,3      |
|o5 : ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     (- H    - H   , - H    - H   H    - H   , - H   H    - H   H    - H   , |
|         1,1    2,1     1,2    1,1 2,1    2,2     1,2 2,1    1,1 2,2    2,3  |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|---------------------------------                                            |
|- H   H    - H   H   , -H   H   )                                            |
|   1,2 2,2    1,1 2,3    1,2 2,3                                             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : chern Q -- The total Chern class of Q, defined as the sum of the Chern c|
|                                                                             |
|o6 = 1 + H    + H    + H                                                     |
|          2,1    2,2    2,3                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|                                            QQ[][H   ..H   , H   ..H   ]     |
|                                                  1,1   1,2   2,1   2,3      |
|o6 : ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     (- H    - H   , - H    - H   H    - H   , - H   H    - H   H    - H   , |
|         1,1    2,1     1,2    1,1 2,1    2,2     1,2 2,1    1,1 2,2    2,3  |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|lasses of Q.                                                                 |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|---------------------------------                                            |
|- H   H    - H   H   , -H   H   )                                            |
|   1,2 2,2    1,1 2,3    1,2 2,3                                             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

If we want to specify a bundle directly by its Chern classes, we can use the
*note abstractSheaf: (Schubert2)abstractSheaf_lpAbstractVariety_cmRingElement_
rp, command:

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : Q = abstractSheaf(G,ChernClass=>1+H_(2,1)+H_(2,2)+H_(2,3),Rank=>3)      |
|                                                                             |
|o7 = Q                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o7 : an abstract sheaf of rank 3 on G                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : chern Q                                                                 |
|                                                                             |
|o8 = 1 + H    + H    + H                                                     |
|          2,1    2,2    2,3                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|                                            QQ[][H   ..H   , H   ..H   ]     |
|                                                  1,1   1,2   2,1   2,3      |
|o8 : ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     (- H    - H   , - H    - H   H    - H   , - H   H    - H   H    - H   , |
|         1,1    2,1     1,2    1,1 2,1    2,2     1,2 2,1    1,1 2,2    2,3  |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|---------------------------------                                            |
|- H   H    - H   H   , -H   H   )                                            |
|   1,2 2,2    1,1 2,3    1,2 2,3                                             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

